mleith@ibm.net writes:

>The one thing I'm not sure about... is why do you want to use your
>dUnix cdrom on another system... it would seem to be of little use.

Presumably because the CDROM drive is installed on another system.
It's considerably easier to mount the CDROM on the system having the
drive and then NFS-mount it on the OSF/1 system, than moving the drive
to the OSF/1 system and trying to get it working there.

Unfortunately, this is not possible because of the ufs issue.  What
exactly prevents the DEC firmware from booting from ISO9660 media, apart
from the lack of support for this filesystem?

Dan
