File an SPR to "make distribution CDROMs in ISO9660 format".  Justify it.
Keep in mind that (a) although distribution media must be readable on
Digital UNIX systems, very few need them readable elsewhere; (b) it
suggests ceasing support for UFS distribution CDROMs because of the
overhead and difficulty of supporting two media formats; and (c) it makes
the firmware more complex, forever.

So is it worth doing?

