Andreas Stumpf (andreas@cubes.s.bawue.de) wrote:
: Hi all,
: I have serious trouble doing Hardware-Handshake on a serial device. I'm using 
: a device which requires RTS-CTS-Handshake and have written a program doing this
: It works fine at my ALPHA-Station 4/166 with OSF 3.0
: Now I've installed the program on another machine (ALPHAserver with digital 
: UNIX 3.2) and the following happens:

:   RTS drops, when the first characters are sent to the device. 

: I have no idea how to influence this behaviour.

The (hardware ?) implementation of the serial ports used in the low-cost ALPAHs
seems to be one of the mysteries out of the DEC dungeons.

Some weeks ago I tried to get a DCF Time-Brick up on a 200/4 without success,
and it turned out that it's not possible to set the 2 control lines of the
serial port (RTS and DTR) independently. Raising one via ioctl() pulls the
other up too. I verified this using a LED-equipped breakout box. As You
obviously have a small test program at hand, i'm asking You to proove my 
observations. BTW on an AIX or a Linux 1.2.x system ;-) everything works o.k.

